.SH NAME
ssoosshd-nss-lookup - Ask the userdb socket exactly as nss-systemd does, for debugging.


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBssoosshd-nss lookup [command] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Calls the daemon's userdb socket the way nss-systemd does and prints each reply's JSON. userdbctl user NAME and getent passwd NAME exercise the same path through systemd.


.SH OPTIONS
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for lookup

.PP
\fB--socket\fP="/run/systemd/userdb/com.github.mnestor.ssoossh"
	the userdb socket


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--admin-socket\fP="/run/ssoossh-nss/admin.sock"
	the admin socket the CLI and the daemon share

.PP
\fB-c\fP, \fB--config\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss.yaml"
	the daemon's configuration file

.PP
\fB--overrides\fP="/etc/ssoossh/nss-overrides.yaml"
	the host override file


